From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-zero2/zero3: keep VDD-SYS at or above 900 mV

On the Orange Pi Zero2 (AXP305 DCDCC) and Zero3 (AXP313a DCDC1) the
"vdd-gpu-sys" rail feeds both the Mali-G31 and the SoC's VDD-SYS
domain, which includes the video engine. With the GPU OPP table in
place, panfrost devfreq drops the rail to 810 mV whenever the GPU is
idle, which the VE does not tolerate at its operating clock: 4K H.265
and VP9 decodes intermittently produce corrupted CTBs (about half of
13 runs at 600 MHz/810 mV; 0 of 6 at 890 mV or 950 mV). The vendor BSP
runs every GPU OPP at 950 mV and so never lowers this rail.

Raise the regulator floor to 900 mV. The OPP entries keep their
<target min max> triplets with a 990 mV maximum, so the regulator core
clamps the low-frequency requests into [900, 990] mV and devfreq keeps
scaling the clock.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts | 2 +-
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@
 
 			reg_dcdcc: dcdcc {
 				regulator-always-on;
-				regulator-min-microvolt = <810000>;
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <900000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <990000>;
 				regulator-name = "vdd-gpu-sys";
 			};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 
 			reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
 				regulator-always-on;
-				regulator-min-microvolt = <810000>;
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <900000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <990000>;
 				regulator-name = "vdd-gpu-sys";
 			};
